title: "stdlib.protobuf Tutorial"
author: IVANLI2412
date: 2026-11-23
abstract: Protocol Buffers encoding/decoding tutorial with varint, zigzag, length-delimited, and message encoding.

# stdlib.protobuf Tutorial

## Quick Start
```lateralus
import "protobuf"
let encoded = protobuf.encode_varint(300)
print(protobuf.bytes_to_hex(encoded))  -- "ac02"
let decoded = protobuf.decode_varint(protobuf.hex_to_bytes("ac02"))
print(decoded)  -- 300
```

## Varint Encoding
- encode_varint(value: int) - bytes: Encodes unsigned integer as protobuf varint
- decode_varint(data: bytes) - int: Decodes varint from bytes

## Zigzag Encoding (for signed integers)
- encode_zigzag(value: int) - int: Maps signed to unsigned
- decode_zigzag(value: int) - int: Maps unsigned back to signed

## Length-Delimited
- encode_length_delimited(data: bytes) - bytes: Length prefix + data
- decode_length_delimited(data: bytes) - bytes: Decode length-delimited

## Message Encoding
- encode_message(fields: dict) - bytes: Encode field_number -> (wire_type, value)
- decode_message(data: bytes) - dict: Decode to field map
